$split_video_fast — scene split via ffmpeg-scaled frame hashes

SUMMARY
  Like $split_video, but reads frames through ffmpeg scaled to width=320 (default)
  before average-hash comparison. Skips OpenCV for decoding — faster on large
  videos. Fragment export still uses ffmpeg (same as $split_video).

SYNTAX
  $split_video_fast
  $split_video_fast(threshold=12, hash_size=8, min_frames=100, width=320)

INPUT
  videos[] — source video files

OUTPUT
  videos[] — one MP4 per fragment (input videos cleared)
  labels[] — one "fragment" entry per output video:
    [ "fragment", [("videos", "<link>")], {"src": "<source_link>", "frame": <start>} ]

ARGUMENTS
  threshold=  — split when abs(hash - prev_hash) > threshold (default 10)
  hash_size=  — average_hash size (default 8)
  min_frames= — merge fragments shorter than this (default 100)
  width=      — ffmpeg scale width for hash frames (default 320)

DEPENDENCIES
  Pillow, imagehash, ffmpeg (no OpenCV).
  uv sync --extra split_video_fast   or   uv sync --extra media + imagehash

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_SPLIT_VIDEO_FAST=1 — placeholder MP4 + labels, no ffmpeg work.

EXAMPLE
  @parts: $file('long_clip.mp4') -> $split_video_fast(threshold=10) -> $save('frag_%04d.mp4')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — replaces videos[] with fragments; manages labels[] directly.
